 "notes": "Calendar day-window long (McConnell-Xu / Quantpedia TOTM window T-1,T+1..T+3 forced intraday-only: long 09:31 -> 15:55, 0.75-ATR stop, one trade/day) with the all-days unconditional long as the built-in control and 10 other windows (opex_week, fomc/fomc_all = Lucca-Moench 09:31->13:55, payday, pre_witch5, pre_holiday, santa, precash short, dow_tuewed). MNQ fixed defaults: MAIN 80 trades / +10,080 / PF 1.93 / Sharpe 1.80; PRIOR 72 / +1,658 / PF 1.21; 2011-2024 620 / +2,202 / PF 1.06 (8 of 14 years negative). MES: MAIN PF 1.71, PRIOR 0.91, 2011-24 0.94. Control (all_days) MAIN: MES PF 1.07 +2,697, MNQ PF 1.14 +10,051 on 430 trades (long-biased tape); 2011-24 PF 0.94 / 1.01. TOTM minus control: 2025-26 +18 (MES) / +22 (MNQ) bp/day, t 2.3 / 2.1; 2011-2024 -0.6 / -0.2 bp, t ~0 -> a two-year streak (55 Mon-Wed trades +12,235 vs Thu/Fri -2,166 on MNQ), no historical counterpart. Walk-forward OOS 2025-01..2026-09 (MNQ): 80 trades, net +5,890, PF 1.49, Sharpe 1.11, 10/21 positive months, maxDD -3,217; every 2025-26 fold chose totm; whole OOS 2023-26 PF 1.11. Lucid on the OOS stream: 5 micros pass 0.24, pass-within-21 0.15, P(first payout) 0.05, exp net +132 but bootstrap lower bound -146 = zero-edge control -> not recommended. Window table (windows.csv): no window meets the flag criterion (>= +8 bp/day over control, t >= 2 on 2011-2024, positive in 2025-26). payday is +11/+14 bp, t 3.0-3.4, PF 1.33 on 2011-2024 but -19/-27 bp (t -2.5) in 2025-26. FOMC morning leg (67 press-conference meetings 2013-2024): intraday +2 bp vs control, t 0.5, PF 1.06/1.27; 2025-26 14 events -519/-1,301, 6 winners; the drift is overnight: prev close -> 09:30 +22/+32 bp, t 3.7/3.9 on the same days. opex_week, pre_witch5 intraday <= 0, overnight +15-28 bp in 2025-26; santa negative everywhere; precash short ~0 (overnight gaps against it); pre_holiday MES +6.7 bp over control (t 1.1) only; trend filter hurts. Grid rank corr MAIN/PRIOR: MES -0.15, MNQ 0.66. Verdict marginal by the WF rule only; the evidence says dead (no edge 2011-2024, Lucid lower bound = zero edge); no calendar +1 bias flag is justified for the other families.",
